<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified" version="2.0">
  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
RESPONSE schema for couponAuthentication (Customer360). Returned in the response body.
Audited 2026-10-12 against the loyalty-app service generation.

Two document roots are possible:
  1. WEBSERVICE/RESPONSE -- every response produced by the operation itself.
  2. bare RESPONSE       -- produced before the operation runs (access-token gate, E899) or by
                            the generic runtime-error page (E999).

How to read the outcome (IMPORTANT):
  - A coupon that was found and evaluated carries NO RESPONSE_CODE. The verdict is
    RESP_STATUS_CODE: COUPON_AVAILABLE (usable), COUPON_EXPIRED, COUPON_REDEEMED (already
    scanned at a POS) or COUPON_AUDITED (redemption already reconciled against an order).
  - Every other outcome carries a RESPONSE_CODE (open string, catalog below), usually with
    RESP_STATUS_CODE = COUPON_UNAVAILABLE, PROMO_UNAVAILABLE, or an EMPTY RESP_STATUS_CODE (E842).

RESPONSE_CODE catalog (kept as xs:string on purpose; new codes must not break validation):
  E101 XmlInput empty       E102 malformed XML      E103 parser configuration   E104 I/O reading input
       (E101-E104 are emitted as a direct child of RESPONSE, after two empty containers)
  E113 promotion is not assigned to the requesting store (RESP_STATUS_CODE COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E115 no store could be resolved
  E116 REQ_COUPON_CODE missing or empty
  E119 the coupon's promotion is not approved or has ended (RESP_STATUS_CODE PROMO_UNAVAILABLE)
  E123 coupon is not yet valid: its start date is in the future (COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E127 REQ_STORE_ID unknown
  E841 coupon code not found (COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E842 REQ_COUPON_TYPE missing or different from the promotion's type (RESP_STATUS_CODE empty)
  E843 coupon usage limit reached (COUPON_UNAVAILABLE)
  E899 accessTokenKey validation failed (bare RESPONSE root)
  E999 unhandled error (bare RESPONSE root, empty RESPONSE_DATE, no ResponseId)

Timestamps are "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" strings, NOT xs:dateTime.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Top-level wrapper for every response produced by the couponAuthentication operation.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Response payload. Echoes the coupon and reports the authentication outcome.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:choice>
              <xs:sequence>
                <xs:element name="RESP_COUPON_DETAILS">
                  <xs:annotation>
                    <xs:documentation>Echo of the coupon that was evaluated. Always present; empty on E101-E104.</xs:documentation>
                  </xs:annotation>
                  <xs:complexType>
                    <xs:sequence>
                      <xs:element name="RESP_COUPON_CODE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>The coupon code exactly as sent in REQ_COUPON_CODE (including any tenant prefix). Empty when no code was sent (E116). Absent on E101-E104.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="RESP_COUPON_TYPE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Echo of REQ_COUPON_TYPE as sent (SERIALIZE or NONSERIALIZE; may be empty). Emitted on evaluated coupons and on E113, E841, E842; absent on E101-E104, E115, E116, E119, E123, E127, E843.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                    </xs:sequence>
                  </xs:complexType>
                </xs:element>
                <!-- NOTE: 'TRANSACTOIN' is a genuine misspelling in the service and is the ONLY spelling emitted. Do NOT correct it; it is the real wire contract. -->
                <xs:element name="RESP_TRANSACTOIN_DETAILS">
                  <xs:annotation>
                    <xs:documentation>Authentication outcome and transaction context. Always present; empty on E101-E104. Modeled as a repeating choice: the subset returned depends on the outcome (see each element).</xs:documentation>
                  </xs:annotation>
                  <xs:complexType>
                    <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                      <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Outcome code; ABSENT when the coupon was found and evaluated (read RESP_STATUS_CODE instead). See the catalog in the schema header.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="RESP_STORE_ID" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Store the coupon was evaluated for: the REQ_STORE_ID sent, or the tenant default store when none was sent. Emitted on evaluated coupons and on E113.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="RESP_DATE" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Server timestamp of the evaluation, format "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" (e.g. 2026-10-12 15:00:02.123). Deliberately xs:string: the format is not ISO 8601. Emitted on evaluated coupons and on E113.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="POS_PROMO_CODE" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>POS-side promotion code configured for the coupon's promotion; empty when none is configured. Emitted (possibly empty) on evaluated coupons and on E113, E841, E842. On E113 only, the service fills this element from the promotion's e-commerce promotion code instead of the POS-side code.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="INT_PROMO_CODE" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Internal promotion identifier the coupon belongs to; empty when the coupon was not found (E841). Emitted on evaluated coupons and on E113, E841, E842.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="PROMOTION_TYPE_ID" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Promotion type. On evaluated coupons the service maps LOYALTY to C7 and MARKETING to C3; ALL and any other type are passed through unchanged. On E113 and E842 the unmapped internal type is returned (e.g. LOYALTY); on E841 it is empty.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="RESP_CUSTOMER_ID" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Reserved. Always emitted EMPTY by the loyalty-app service generation.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="RESP_STATUS_CODE" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Status of the coupon. Deliberately xs:string (a closed list previously rejected live values). Values emitted: COUPON_AVAILABLE (valid and usable); COUPON_EXPIRED (past its end date plus grace period); COUPON_REDEEMED (already scanned at a POS); COUPON_AUDITED (redemption reconciled against an order); COUPON_UNAVAILABLE (with E113, E123, E841, E843); PROMO_UNAVAILABLE (with E119); EMPTY (with E842). Absent on E101-E104, E115, E116, E127.</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="RESP_AUTH_CODE" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>Reserved. Always emitted EMPTY by the loyalty-app service generation (on evaluated coupons and on E113).</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="ATG_PROMO_CODE" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>NOT emitted by the loyalty-app service generation. Retained from the earlier published schema so documents from an older service generation still validate (older behaviour not verified).</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                      <xs:element name="SYSTEM_REFERENCE_ID" type="xs:string">
                        <xs:annotation>
                          <xs:documentation>NOT emitted by the loyalty-app service generation. Retained from the earlier published schema so documents from an older service generation still validate (older behaviour not verified).</xs:documentation>
                        </xs:annotation>
                      </xs:element>
                    </xs:choice>
                  </xs:complexType>
                </xs:element>
                <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                  <xs:annotation>
                    <xs:documentation>Input-level failure code E101-E104 only. These four codes are emitted here, as a direct child of RESPONSE after the two (empty) containers, not inside RESP_TRANSACTOIN_DETAILS.</xs:documentation>
                  </xs:annotation>
                </xs:element>
              </xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Gate-error envelope of the older service generation (E888 / E899): RESPONSE carries this element alone, with no containers and no ResponseId.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
              </xs:element>
            </xs:choice>
            <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>Request-log correlation id generated by the service for this call. Quote it when reporting an issue.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
            </xs:attribute>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Bare RESPONSE root (no WEBSERVICE wrapper). Used only for failures raised outside the operation: E899 (accessTokenKey validation failed; carries ResponseId and a RESPONSE_DATE timestamp) and E999 (unhandled error; RESPONSE_DATE is an EMPTY element and there is no ResponseId).</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Server timestamp "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" on E899; empty on E999.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>E899 or E999.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Request-log correlation id. Present on E899; absent on E999.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
